{"ref":"BDB, יָאִיר","hw":"יָאִיר","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">יָאִיר</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.m. (</strong><em>he enlightens</em>, or <em>one giving light</em><strong>)</strong>.<br><strong>1.</strong>  son of Manasseh <a data-ref=\"Numbers 32:41\" href=\"/Numbers.32.41\">Nu 32:41</a><sup>(×2)</sup> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 3:14\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.3.14\">Dt 3:14</a><sup>(×2)</sup> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 13:30\" href=\"/Joshua.13.30\">Jos 13:30</a> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 4:13\" href=\"/I_Kings.4.13\">1 K 4:13</a> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 2:22\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.2.22\">1 Ch 2:22</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 2:23\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.2.23\">23</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  a judge in Gilead <a data-ref=\"Judges 10:3\" href=\"/Judges.10.3\">Ju 10:3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 10:4\" href=\"/Judges.10.4\">4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 10:5\" href=\"/Judges.10.5\">5</a>.<br><strong>3.</strong>  father of Mordecai <a data-ref=\"Esther 2:5\" href=\"/Esther.2.5\">Est 2:5</a>.","next":"BDB, יָאִירִי","prev":"BDB, אוּרִיָּ֫הוּ"}